---
description: Spring Boot DevOps and CI/CD Rules
globs: "Dockerfile*,docker-compose*.yml,Jenkinsfile,.dockerignore"
alwaysApply: true
---

# Spring Boot Docker Rules

- ALWAYS use multi-stage Docker builds
- Use eclipse-temurin:21-jdk-alpine for build stage
- Use eclipse-temurin:21-jre-alpine for runtime stage
- Optimize Docker layer caching
- Copy pom.xml before source code
- Run Maven dependency download before copying source
- Use Maven wrapper if available
- Skip tests during Docker image build using:
  mvn clean package -DskipTests
- Final image should be lightweight
- Expose application port 8082
- Use ENTRYPOINT instead of CMD

# Dockerfile Standards

- Builder stage name must be: builder
- Runtime stage name must be: runtime
- Application jar should be copied as app.jar
- Final command:

  ENTRYPOINT ["java","-jar","/app/app.jar"]

# Docker Compose Rules

- Generate docker-compose.yml if requested
- Include:
  - backend service
  - mysql service if project uses database
- Use restart: always
- Add healthcheck for backend
- Use bridge network
- Use environment variables
- Map port 8080:8080

# Jenkinsfile Rules

- Use declarative Jenkins pipeline
- Stages:
  - Checkout
  - Build
  - Test
  - Docker Build
  - Docker Run or Push
- Use clean workspace after build
- Fail pipeline on test failure
- Use Docker agent if possible
- Tag docker image with BUILD_NUMBER
- Archive artifacts after build

# Security Rules

- Never hardcode passwords
- Use Jenkins credentials
- Use environment variables for secrets

# Output Rules

- Generate complete production-ready files
- Include comments explaining important sections
- Keep formatting clean and readable
